 "final_summary": "The bug was in the retry logic where every retry used the base delay instead of exponential backoff. The fix changed `delays[0]` to `delays[attempt]` in the retry loop and ensured the final attempt raises the exception. This now correctly implements the backoff schedule as specified in the API contract.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/retry.py b/tracker/retry.py\nindex 8a6a89a..c17bee0 100644\n--- a/tracker/retry.py\n+++ b/tracker/retry.py\n@@ -27,4 +27,4 @@ def retry_call(func, attempts=3, base_delay=0.05, sleep=time.sleep, retry_on=(Tr\n         except retry_on:\n             if attempt == attempts - 1:\n                 raise\n-            sleep(delays[0])\n+            sleep(delays[attempt])\n",
